   142	## 3. Task (1): one order deeper, on the wall itself
   143	
   144	### 3.1 The wall in closed form
   145	
   146	Wall B is `G_{2e} = -b(1+2e) eta_e^2`, equivalently `deg E1 <= 2e-1` for
   147	`E1 = (b Z eta^2)' + G`. Treating `E1` rather than `G` as the free object makes
   148	the whole live system collapse. With `psi = (Z eta)'`, `chi = eta + 2Z eta'`,
   149	`phi = eta + 3Z eta'`, `d = 3a/2b` and `Theta := s E1/eta`:
   150	
   151	```text
   152	   G   = E1 - b(Z eta^2)'                                          (definition)
   153	   D1  = -a eta^3 / 2 + d eta E1            [ since phi - (3/2)chi = -eta/2 ]
   154	   Phi = s G/eta = -b s chi + Theta
   155	   C1  = (d/2) ( s eta + Theta/b )          [ since psi - chi/2 = eta/2 ]
   156	   T1's divisibility  eta | sG   <==>   eta | s E1 .
   157	```
   158	
   159	Two consequences. First, `deg D1 = 3e` with leader `-a eta_e^3/2` and
   160	`deg C1 = e+sigma` with leader `d eta_e s_sigma/2`: both survive Wall B, so no
   161	further branch hides there. Second, in these variables
   162	
   163	```text
   164	 EQ1 = -3a eta^3 r' + d s(s'eta - s eta')                     [E1-free, top]
   165	       + 6d eta E1 r' - 4q'E1 + 2q E1' + (d/b)(2 Theta s' - s Theta')
   166	       + 2 kappa Z ,
   167	 EQ4 =  d s^2 eta r' + q s s' - q' s^2                        [E1-free, top]
   168	       + (d/b) s Theta r' - 2 q E1 r' + kappa E1 ,
   169	```
   170	
   171	so **every** term of `EQ1` and of `EQ4` carries `r'`, `q` or `s`: neither
   172	equation has a pure `eta/G` family. `EQ3` and `EQ2` do, at `u = 3e-1`.
   173	
   174	### 3.2 The grading, and where the boundary is
   175	
   176	With `m = U`, `n = U-e`, `2 sigma = U+e` (so `U ≡ e mod 2`, hence `n` even,
   177	`n >= 2e`), every family of `EQ3` sits at degree `(3e+1)+u`, of `EQ1` at
   178	`(2e-1)+u`, of `EQ2` at `2e+u`, with `u_r = u_q = u_s = U` and
   179	`u_eta = u_G = u_T = 3e-1` in Chamber II. Because `U - 3e` is always even, the
   180	`eta/G/target` families sit at
   181	
   182	```text
   183	   top - (U - 3e + 1) ,      an ODD offset:  top-1, top-3, top-5, ...
   184	```
   185	
   186	They therefore hit `top-1` **exactly when `U = 3e`**, and never hit `top-2`.
   187	That single arithmetic fact organises everything below: the boundary slice
   188	`U = 3e` is inhomogeneous at the next order, every other cell is homogeneous.
   189	
   190	Each order-`(top-k)` coefficient is linear in the `k`-th coefficients of
   191	`eta,s,q,r,G`, so at `k = 1` the only possible inhomogeneous term comes from a
   192	family whose own top sits at `top-1`. On Wall B the `E1`-carrying families of
   193	`EQ1` and `EQ4` do sit there, but contribute linearly in `E1_{2e-1}`, itself
   194	linear in the second coefficients. Hence:
   195	
   196	> **STRUCTURE.** For `U >= 3e+2` the order-`(top-1)` system is linear and
   197	> **homogeneous**; it cannot be contradictory. For `U = 3e` it is
   198	> inhomogeneous, and that is the only place a contradiction can live at this
   199	> order.
   200	
   201	This answers the charge's first disjunct with a reason rather than with a
   202	failed search: away from the boundary slice, no next-order contradiction
   203	exists, for structural reasons.
   204	
   205	### 3.3 THEOREM RAY-1: the four next-order conditions
   206	
   207	Put, on the ray,
   208	
   209	```text
   210	  alpha = eta_{e-1}/eta_e ,  beta = s_{sigma-1}/s_sigma ,  gamma = q_{m-1}/q_m ,
   211	  delta = r_{n-1}/r_n ,      epshat = G_{2e-1}/(b eta_e^2) .
   212	```
   213	
   214	> **THEOREM RAY-1.** On Wall B in the simultaneous-top regime `U >= 3e`, the
   215	> order-`(top-1)` coefficient conditions of `EQ3, EQ1, EQ2, EQ4` are exactly
   216	>
   217	> ```text
   218	>  (N3)  beta - gamma + delta/2                                        = rho
   219	>  (N1)  alpha - beta + delta/2                                        = 0
   220	>  (N4)  n*alpha - 2*beta - (n-2)*gamma + (n-1)*delta                  = 0
   221	>  (N2)  (2n-2e-3)alpha - 2(3n+2e-4)beta + (4n+2e-5)gamma
   222	>                                     - (n-1)delta - epshat            = 0
   223	> ```
   224	> with
   225	> ```text
   226	>    rho = 0                                                if U >= 3e+2,
   227	>    rho = (32e^3+32e^2+6e+1) b^2 eta_e^4 / ((4e-2) s_sigma^2)   if U = 3e.
   228	> ```
   229	> The normalising factors are `EQ3 = 6(n-1)(a/b) eta_e^2 s_sigma^2 * (N3)`,
   230	> `EQ1 = -(3/2)(n-1)(a/b) eta_e s_sigma^2 * (N1)`,
   231	> `EQ4 = (3a/8b^2)(s_sigma^4/eta_e) * (N4)`.
   232	
   233	`(N1)`, `(N3)`, `(N4)` are **derived by hand** in the closed form of Sec 3.1
   234	(the derivations are reproduced in Sec 3.4-3.5 in compressed form) and then
   235	checked against the CAS at ten cells with the displayed normalising factors:
   236	exact agreement, `rho` sign included. `(N2)` is **measured**: its closed form
   237	was interpolated from the CAS and verified, together with `(N1),(N3),(N4)` and
   238	`rho`, at all 50 cells `1 <= e <= 10`, `U in {3e, 3e+2, ..., 3e+8}`, with zero
   239	mismatches. A wider 72-cell sweep (`1 <= e <= 12`, `U in {3e, ..., 3e+10}`)
   240	confirms at every cell: `rank = 3`, kernel contained in `{E1_{2e-1} = 0}`,
   241	`rho` as displayed, and consistency exactly when `U >= 3e+2`.
   242	
   243	Two structural facts fall out of the hand derivations and deserve display,
   244	because they are what makes the system rank-deficient.
   245	
   246	* In `EQ1` the `E1_{2e-1}` contributions from `6d eta E1 r'`, `-4q'E1+2qE1'`
   247	  and `(d/b)(2 Theta s' - s Theta')` sum, on the ray, to a multiple of
   248	  `3(n + e - U) = 0`. **They cancel identically.**
   249	* In `EQ4` the two `E1_{2e-1}` contributions, from `(d/b) s Theta r'` and from
   250	  `-2 q E1 r'`, are exact negatives on the ray. **They cancel identically.**
   251	
   252	So `epshat` occurs in `(N2)` only: the wall's own deviation is invisible to
   253	three of the four conditions.
   254	
   255	### 3.4 THEOREM RAY-DEP and the kill of the boundary slice
   256	
   257	> **THEOREM RAY-DEP.** Identically in `(alpha,beta,gamma,delta,rho,n)`,
   258	> ```text
   259	>      n*(N1) + (n-2)*(N3) - (N4)  =  -(n-2)*rho .
   260	> ```
   261	> *Proof.* The `beta`-coefficient is `-n + (n-2) + 2 = 0`; the `gamma`
   262	> coefficient is `-(n-2) + (n-2) = 0`; the `delta` coefficient is
   263	> `n/2 + (n-2)/2 - (n-1) = 0`; `alpha` cancels between `n*(N1)` and `-(N4)`.
   264	> The only survivor is `-(n-2) rho`. QED
   265	
   266	> **THEOREM RAY-EDGE.** The boundary slice `U = 3e` of the E1-wall is EMPTY.
   267	>
   268	> *Proof for `e >= 2`.* At `U = 3e` one has `n = 2e >= 4`, so `n - 2 != 0`, and
   269	> `rho != 0` because `32e^3+32e^2+6e+1 > 0` for `e >= 1`. By RAY-DEP the four
   270	> next-order conditions are inconsistent. QED
   271	>
   272	> The remaining cell is `n = 2`. Since `n = U - e` and `U >= 3e` force
   273	> `n >= 2e`, `n = 2` happens **only** at `(e,U) = (1,3)`, which is killed in
   274	> Sec 3.7. QED
   275	
   276	The obstruction `rho` is not a new quantity. Let
   277	`P(c) := 4e^2(2e-1) + 4ce(2e-1) - c^2(6e+1)` be HF's own Chamber II
   278	coincidence polynomial (HF Sec 4.4, `U < 3e-1` branch). Then
   279	
   280	```text
   281	   P(-(2e+1)) = -(32e^3 + 32e^2 + 6e + 1) ,
   282	   rho        = -P(-(2e+1)) * b^2 eta_e^4 / ((4e-2) s_sigma^2) .
   283	```
   284	
   285	HR Sec 7.5 records `P(-(2e+1)) != 0` as the reason Wall B and the `U < 3e-1`
   286	wall are different walls. **The same nonvanishing now kills the boundary slice
   287	of Wall B itself**: the coincident `eta/G/target` families, which at `U = 3e`
   288	sit one order below the top, contribute `P` at Wall B, and there is no
   289	remaining freedom to absorb it.
   290	
   291	*Derivation sketch for `(N3)`.* At `top-1`, `EQ3`'s `r,q,s` families give,
   292	after the ray substitution and division by `a s_sigma^2 eta_e^2/b`, the columns
   293	`alpha: 12n - 6(3n+1) + 6(n+1) = 0`, `beta: 6(n-1)`, `gamma: -6(n-1)`,
   294	`delta: 3(n-1)`; so `EQ3|_{top-1} = 6(n-1)(a/b) eta_e^2 s_sigma^2 (beta - gamma
   295	+ delta/2)` plus, when `U = 3e`, the coincident-family term
   296	`3ab eta_e^6 P(-(2e+1))`. The vanishing `alpha` column is the source of the
   297	rank drop.
   298	
   299	### 3.5 THEOREM RAY-2: the wall tightens
   300	
   301	> **THEOREM RAY-2.** On every surviving cell the next order forces
   302	> ```text
   303	>       E1_{2e-1} = 0 ,   i.e.   deg E1 <= 2e - 2 .
   304	> ```
   305	> *Proof.* `(N1)` and `(N3)` with `rho = 0` give `alpha = beta - delta/2` and
   306	> `gamma = beta + delta/2`. Substituting into `(N2)`:
   307	> the `beta` column is `(2n-2e-3) - 2(3n+2e-4) + (4n+2e-5) = -4e`, and the
   308	> `delta` column is `-(2n-2e-3)/2 + (4n+2e-5)/2 - (n-1) = 2e`, so
   309	> `epshat = -4e beta + 2e delta = -4e(beta - delta/2) = -4e alpha`. Since
   310	> `E1_{2e-1} = b eta_e^2 (4e alpha + epshat)`, it vanishes. QED
   311	
   312	At `e = 1` this says `deg E1 <= 0`: on the surviving `e = 1` cells `E1` is a
   313	**constant**. (`RAY-2` inherits `(N2)`'s MEASURED typing; `(N1)`,`(N3)` are
   314	hand-derived.)
   315	
   316	### 3.6 The exact residual, and order `top-2`
   317	
   318	For `U >= 3e+2` the next-order solution set is 2-dimensional, parametrised by
   319	`(beta, delta)`:
   320	
   321	```text
   322	   eta_{e-1}/eta_e = beta - delta/2 ,      s_{sigma-1}/s_sigma = beta ,
   323	   q_{m-1}/q_m     = beta + delta/2 ,      r_{n-1}/r_n         = delta ,
   324	   G_{2e-1}        = -4 e b eta_e eta_{e-1} ,
   325	```
   326	
   327	i.e. `eta_{e-1}/eta_e + q_{m-1}/q_m = 2 s_{sigma-1}/s_sigma` and
   328	`q_{m-1}/q_m - eta_{e-1}/eta_e = r_{n-1}/r_n`.
   329	
   330	**Order `top-2`.** By Sec 3.2 no `eta/G/target` family reaches `top-2`, so the
   331	order-`(top-2)` system is four conditions on the five third coefficients
   332	`(eta_{e-2}, s_{sigma-2}, q_{m-2}, r_{n-2}, G_{2e-2})` with an inhomogeneity
   333	quadratic in `(beta,delta)`. Computed with the next-order solution substituted:
   334	
   335	```text
   336	   U >= 3e+2  (10 cells, e <= 5): rank 3, and the augmented matrix has rank 3
   337	                                  too, for ALL (beta,delta).
   338	                                  ==> NO new condition.  Residual grows.
   339	   (e,U) = (1,3):                 rank 2, cokernel of dimension 2, giving the
   340	                                  single condition  426 eta_1^6 a b (2 beta - delta) = 0,
   341	                                  i.e.  delta = 2 beta,  i.e.  alpha = 0,
   342	                                  i.e.  eta = eta_1 Z .   (426 = 6 * 71 and
   343	                                  71 = 32e^3+32e^2+6e+1 at e = 1.)
   344	```
   345	
   346	So the order-by-order ladder does **not** terminate on the surviving cells: four
   347	conditions against five new unknowns per order, with the fifth unknown running
   348	out only when a polynomial's coefficients are exhausted. Any further kill must
   349	be a per-cell finiteness argument, not a further leading-order pass. That is
   350	Task (2).
   351	
   352	### 3.7 The degenerate cell `(e,U) = (1,3)`: EMPTY, exactly
   353	
   354	`(1,3)` is the unique cell where `n = 2` and RAY-DEP is vacuous, and it is
   355	small enough to decide outright: `e=1, sigma=2, m=3, n=2, g=2`, `deg Phi = 3`,
   356	`deg p' = 2`; 22 unknowns after the legal normalisations `a = b = 1` (S1) and
   357	`eta_e = 1` (S2), including `kappa` and one saturation variable. Generators:
   358	the coefficientwise vanishing of
   359	
   360	```text
   361	   EQ1, EQ2, EQ3, EQ4 ,      T1 as  eta*Phi - s*G = 0  (Phi a new polynomial),
   362	   E0  as  2(q r' - p' s) - kappa = 0 ,
   363	   saturation  s_sigma * q_m * r_n * kappa * tt - 1 = 0 .
   364	```
   365	
   366	37 generators. Ideal component extracted as the sympy `GroebnerBasis` over
   367	`Q[22 vars]`, grevlex.
   368	
   369	```text
   370	   RESULT.  The Groebner basis is [1].   The cell (1,3) is EMPTY.        2.2 s
   371	   With the wall G_2 = -3 eta_1^2 NOT imposed (23 unknowns):  also [1].  13.2 s
   372	```
   373	
   374	The second run matters: `(1,3)` is empty independently of the wall derivation,
   375	so this cell does not rest on HORN-A2 at all.
   376	
   377	**Controls on the decision** (FALLACY-v2 `sat()` clause).
