   235	planted control: 37 generators, 22 vars, planted point verified a zero
   236	PLANTED ideal is unit? False
   237	TRUE    ideal is unit? True
   238	```
   239	
   240	So the operational Groebner claim is confirmed: the available sympy
   241	transcription returns the unit ideal.
   242	
   243	Transcription check:
   244	
   245	* `EQ1` in the driver is C32 `(1.1)`, matching `C32:99-105`.
   246	* `EQ3` is `eta Z^2 Xi - (3a/b)(Z eta^2 G^2)'`, matching `C32:241-255`.
   247	* `EQ4` is C32 `(2.2)` from `O0+E0`, matching `C32:586-590`.
   248	* `T1` is implemented as `eta*Phi-s*G=0`, avoiding division by `eta`; this
   249	  matches `C32:177-203`.
   250	* `EQ2` in the driver matches the C32 displayed `E2eq|_{G=0}+Delta_2`
   251	  formula at `C32:631-642`.
   252	
   253	Against `RAY:146-157`, the closed Wall-B identities also check:
   254	
   255	```text
   256	E1 = b eta chi + G
   257	G  = E1 - b eta chi
   258	D1 = a eta^2 phi + d eta G
   259	   = a eta^2(phi - 3chi/2) + d eta E1
   260	   = -a eta^3/2 + d eta E1
   261	
   262	C1 = d(psi s + Phi/(2b)),  Phi=sG/eta
   263	   = d(psi s + sE1/(2b eta) - s chi/2)
   264	   = (d/2)(s eta + Theta/b),  Theta=sE1/eta.
   265	```
   266	
   267	The only caveat is archival: `EQ2` is not fully printed in the two frozen
   268	inputs.  It is printed in the local C32 report whose hash matches the charged
   269	lane receipt, but a future standalone replay should freeze that file or embed
